L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,The fiscal year of the Company commences on April 1 and ends on March 31 of each year
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,"For example, “fiscal 2026” refers to the year commenced on April 1, 2025 and ended on March 31, 2026. . . 4"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,It requires that a public company must be formed by seven (7) or more persons and can be either - (a) a company limited by shares; or (b) a company limited by guarantee; or (c) an unlimited company
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,• to grant loans or give guarantee or provide security in respect of loans;
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,"All surplus assets after payments to the employees, secured creditors, unsecured creditors and preference shareholders are paid to the holders of equity shares in proportion to the amount paid up or credited as paid up on such shares respectively, at the commencement of winding up"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,"The Bank is listed on the ‘National Stock Exchange of India Limited’ and the ‘BSE Ltd’, and has entered into listing agreements with these exchanges pursuant to the commencement of the Listing Regulations"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,The holding period of an equity share received upon the surrender of an ADS will commence on the date on which request for such redemption of the ADS was made
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,The holding period in case of bonus shares will commence from the date of allotment of such bonus shares
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,Our equity shares are compulsorily delivered in non-physical form
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"In India, the insured deposit calculations are based on guidelines prescribed by Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"The insured amount limit prescribed by Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation is up to a maximum amount of Rs. 500,000 per depositor (including all types of deposits), per insured bank"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,term_years,5.0,years,,,Due within 1 year Due between 1 to 5 year Due between 5 to 15 years Due in more than 15 years
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,term_years,5.0,years,,,Due within 1 year Due between 1 to 5 year Due between 5 to 15 years Due in more than 15 years Total
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,"Our commercial banking operations for retail customers consist of retail lending and deposits, and fee-based products and services like credit, debit and prepaid cards and depositary share accounts"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,"We offer several card-based products such as credit cards, debit cards, prepaid cards, travel cards and commercial cards"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,Our transaction banking solutions are delivered to our customers through physical and digital channels and a team of account managers
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Our corporate loan portfolio consists of term loan products and working capital financing in the form of cash credit facilities, overdraft, demand loans and non-fund-based facilities including bill discounting, letters of credit and guarantees"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"We also offer our corporate customers a wide variety of fee and commission-based products and services including documentary credits, standby letters of credit (called guarantees in India), collection and payment of export/import bills and cash management services, including collection, payment and remittance services"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,"Our overseas branches are funded by bond issuances, bilateral loans from banks, loans from export credit agencies, money market borrowings, deposits and refinance from banks"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,3900.0,$M,,,"The corporate fund and non-fund outstanding, net of cash/bank/insurance backed lending, was U.S.$ 3.9 billion at March 31, 2026"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,3900.0,$M,,,"Out of U.S.$ 3.9 billion, 94.2% of the outstanding was to Indian corporates and their subsidiaries and joint ventures and 4.9% of the outstanding was to non-India companies with Indian or India-linked operations and activities and this portfolio is generally well-rated and the Indian operations of these companies are our target customers for deposit and transaction banking franchise"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,265.0,$M,,,"The overseas corporate portfolio, excluding Indian corporates and their subsidiaries and joint ventures, reduced by 16.1% from about U.S.$ 265 million year-on-year to U.S.$ 223 million at March 31, 2026"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,223.0,$M,,,"The overseas corporate portfolio, excluding Indian corporates and their subsidiaries and joint ventures, reduced by 16.1% from about U.S.$ 265 million year-on-year to U.S.$ 223 million at March 31, 2026"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Our subsidiary in Canada originates residential mortgages, primarily insured and qualifying for insurance by either the Canadian federal government agency or insurance companies backstopped by the Canadian federal government and offers loans to both Canadian and U.S. corporations as well as Indian corporations seeking to develop their business overseas"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,contract_value,2900.0,$M,,,"At year-end fiscal 2026, the total assets of ICICI Bank UK PLC were U.S.$ 2.9 billion"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,25.0,$M,,,"ICICI Bank UK PLC made a net profit of U.S.$ 25 million during fiscal 2026, compared to U.S.$ 27 million during fiscal 2025"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,27.0,$M,,,"ICICI Bank UK PLC made a net profit of U.S.$ 25 million during fiscal 2026, compared to U.S.$ 27 million during fiscal 2025"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,financing_or_capex,1500.0,$M,,,"At year-end fiscal 2026, loans and advances of ICICI Bank UK PLC were U.S.$ 1.5 billion and investments were U.S.$ 0.9 billion"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,900.0,$M,,,"At year-end fiscal 2026, loans and advances of ICICI Bank UK PLC were U.S.$ 1.5 billion and investments were U.S.$ 0.9 billion"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Corporate finance loans can be secured by fixed assets (which normally consists of property, plant and equipment), pledge of financial assets (such as marketable securities or at times non-marketable securities) and we may obtain contractual credit enhancements such as corporate guarantees or personal guarantees from the sponsors wherever appropriate"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Additionally, in certain cases, we obtain contractual credit enhancements such as personal guarantees or corporate guarantees from sponsors, or subordinated security interests in the tangible assets of the borrower including plant and machinery"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"In view of the margin rules for non-centrally cleared derivative transactions issued by the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision, guidelines issued by the Reserve Bank of India and guidelines issued by overseas regulators, certain derivative transactions are subject to margining and collateral exchange in accordance with a Credit Support Annex"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,We may also take security of a pledge of financial assets like marketable securities and obtain corporate guarantees and personal guarantees and sponsors wherever appropriate
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Additionally, in some cases, we may take further security on fixed assets, a pledge of financial assets like marketable securities, or obtain corporate guarantees and personal guarantees of sponsors wherever appropriate"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,FASTag is an electronic toll collection system in India operated by the National Highways Authority of India through prepaid radio frequency identification tags
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"The platform facilitates wide range of services such as regularization of bill of entry and export bills, accessing letters of credit and bank guarantees including fixed deposits backed, export credit facility, and facilitating import and export bill collections digitally"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,"For customers utilizing e-commerce platforms, we offer solutions such as digital wallets, prepaid cards and co-branded credit cards"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,There are separate guidelines for classification of loans for projects under implementation which are based on the date of commencement of commercial production and date of completion of the project as originally envisaged at the time of financial closure
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,power_cost,1,flag,,,Banks may also invest in security receipts or pass-through certificates issued by an asset reconstruction company or trusts set up by it to acquire the financial assets
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,Regulations Governing Prepaid Payment Instruments
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,The Reserve Bank of India has issued master directions on the issuance of prepaid payment instruments and operations related to their use
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,"Issuers of such instruments are required to have board-approved policies on: the issuance of prepaid instruments, the engagement of agents for the purpose of issuing and reloading prepaid instruments, co-branding arrangements, gift instruments and related activities"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Demand and time deposits accepted by Indian banks must be insured with the Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation, a wholly owned subsidiary of the Reserve Bank of India"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,Banks are required to pay an insurance premium to the Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation on a semi-annual basis
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,10.0,$M,,,"The Reserve Bank of India also allows banks to borrow funds from their overseas branches and correspondent banks (including borrowings for financing export credit, external commercial borrowings and overdrafts from their head office/nostro account) up to a limit of 100.0% of unimpaired Tier 1 capital or U.S.$ 10 million, whichever is higher"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,"The Government of India, after considering the application of the Reserve Bank of India, may order a moratorium staying commencement of action or proceedings against such banking company for a maximum period of six months"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,power_cost,1,flag,,,"Any increase in inflation, due to increase in domestic food prices or global prices of commodities, including crude oil, the impact of currency depreciation on the prices of imported commodities and additional pass through of higher fuel prices to consumers, or otherwise, may result in a tightening of monetary policy"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,16600.0,$M,,,"In fiscal 2026, net outflows of foreign portfolio investments (“FPI”) from India were U.S. $ 16.6 billion compared to inflows of U.S. $ 2.7 billion in fiscal 2025"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,2700.0,$M,,,"In fiscal 2026, net outflows of foreign portfolio investments (“FPI”) from India were U.S. $ 16.6 billion compared to inflows of U.S. $ 2.7 billion in fiscal 2025"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,power_cost,1,flag,,,"If elevated oil price levels or volatility in oil prices continues, as well as the impact of currency depreciation, which makes imports more expensive in local currency, and the pass-through of such increases to Indian consumers or an increase in subsidies (which would increase the fiscal deficit) there could be a material adverse impact on the Indian economy and the Indian banking and financial system, including through a rise in inflation and market interest rates, higher trade and fiscal deficits and currency depreciation"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"The Reserve Bank of India and other regulators regularly review our operations, and there can be no guarantee that all regulators will agree with our internal assessments of asset quality, provisions, risk management, capital adequacy and management functioning, other measures of the safety and soundness of our operations or compliance with applicable laws, regulations, accounting and taxation norms, listing norms or policies"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"The Reserve Bank of India regularly reviews our operations, and there can be no guarantee that it will agree with our internal assessments of capital adequacy"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"In April 2026, the Reserve Bank of India, issued directions which introduced an expected credit loss framework for provisioning by banks, broadly based on the principles of the International Financial Reporting Standard 9, supplemented by regulatory backstops"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"As an example, following the outbreak of the first wave of the Covid-19 pandemic, the Government of India and the Reserve Bank of India announced several measures during fiscal 2021, including a moratorium on loan repayments for certain borrowers and an asset classification standstill benefit for overdue accounts where a moratorium had been granted, restructuring of loans to small borrowers, including individuals, small businesses and micro, small and medium enterprises (“MSMEs”), and funding under the Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme for MSMEs and other stressed sectors"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Our portfolio includes lending under the Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme and loans where a resolution plan had been implemented and loans to borrowers who had availed moratorium, that may carry higher risks compared to our overall portfolio"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"The Government of India has announced a new emergency credit line guarantee scheme in May 2026 to provide credit guarantee coverage to eligible enterprises, by extending support in terms of additional facilities enabling these entities to navigate any short-term liquidity mismatches"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,Lending under emergency credit line guarantee scheme that may carry higher risks relative to our overall portfolio and past performance may not be indicative for the future
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,rfs,1,flag,,,"The Reserve Bank of India has issued directions on financing of projects in infrastructure and non-infrastructure, including commercial real estate and commercial real estate-residential housing, which inter alia requires rationalization of standard asset provisioning requirement to 1.0% for projects under construction and shall gradually increase for each quarter of ‘date of commencement of commercial operations’ deferment"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,fitout,1,flag,,,"Our international branches are primarily funded by debt capital market issuances and syndicated/bilateral loans, while our international subsidiaries generally raise deposits in their local markets"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,power_cost,1,flag,,,These include borrowers impacted by higher rupee denominated interest or principal repayment on unhedged foreign currency borrowings; increases in the cost of raw material imports where there is limited ability to pass through such escalations to customers; the escalation of project costs due to higher imported equipment costs; and borrowers that may have taken adverse positions in the foreign exchange markets
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"We cannot guarantee that the judgments in, or the outcomes of any of the litigation or other proceedings or of any settlement or compounding of legal or regulatory proceedings in which we are involved would be favorable to us and if our assessment of the risk changes, our view on provisions will also change"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,credit_support,1,flag,,,"While we have procedures to monitor for and prevent system downtime or failures, and to recover from system failures in the event they occur, there is no guarantee that these procedures will successfully prevent a system failure or allow us to recover quickly from a system failure"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,446100.0,$M,,,India’s merchandise exports were broadly flat at U.S. $ 446.1 billion in fiscal 2026 compared to U.S. $ 442.1 billion in fiscal 2025
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,442100.0,$M,,,India’s merchandise exports were broadly flat at U.S. $ 446.1 billion in fiscal 2026 compared to U.S. $ 442.1 billion in fiscal 2025
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,783400.0,$M,,,Merchandise imports on the other hand rose by 7.5% year-on-year to U.S. $ 783.4 billion in fiscal 2026 compared to U.S. $ 729.0 billion in fiscal 2025
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,729000.0,$M,,,Merchandise imports on the other hand rose by 7.5% year-on-year to U.S. $ 783.4 billion in fiscal 2026 compared to U.S. $ 729.0 billion in fiscal 2025
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,337300.0,$M,,,"The trade deficit, hence, rose to U.S. $ 337.3 billion in fiscal 2026 as compared to U.S. $ 286.9 billion in fiscal 2025"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,286900.0,$M,,,"The trade deficit, hence, rose to U.S. $ 337.3 billion in fiscal 2026 as compared to U.S. $ 286.9 billion in fiscal 2025"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,216600.0,$M,,,"However, net services exports have seen an increase to U.S. $ 216.6 billion in fiscal 2026 as compared to U.S. $ 188.8 billion in fiscal 2025"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,188800.0,$M,,,"However, net services exports have seen an increase to U.S. $ 216.6 billion in fiscal 2026 as compared to U.S. $ 188.8 billion in fiscal 2025"
L000095010326014340_dp253614_6k,usd_other,25400.0,$M,,,India’s current account deficit stood at U.S. $ 25.4 billion or 0.6% of GDP in fiscal 2026
