L000108330124000102_wulfinvestorpresentation,mw_unspecified,300.0,MW,more than,unspecified,Lowest-cost producer of Bitcoin with large-scale infrastructure optionality ➢ Existing sites have more than 300 MW of available capacity to expand ➢ Attractive site strategically positioned to support other forms of compute ➢ Achieved $0.032/kWh all-in power cost in 2023 ➢ Target $0.035/kWh all-in power cost in 2024 ➢ Recent 7 EH/s purchase and option agreement for S21 miners ➢ Locks in pricing at ~$16 per terahash ➢ Reduced debt by 50% in the last 6 months with free cash flow generation ➢ 2024 growth plan largely funded; expect to be debt free in 2025 with substantial free cash flow to reinvest in business
