L000108330126000026_a_wulfearningsrelease2026-,mw_it,162.0,MW,,it,"Through design optimization across later phases, critical IT capacity for CB4 and CB5 increased from 162 MW to 168 MW per building without increasing base construction budgets, enhancing long-term lease revenue potential. . “These projects reflect disciplined construction execution and close coordination with our hyperscale stakeholder and customers,” said Nazar Khan, Chief Technology Officer. . “Our teams are advancing build schedules, integrating tenant fit-out requirements, and optimizing cooling, electrical, and design architecture to support next-generation AI workloads at scale.”"
L000108330126000026_a_wulfearningsrelease2026-,mw_it,168.0,MW,,it,"Through design optimization across later phases, critical IT capacity for CB4 and CB5 increased from 162 MW to 168 MW per building without increasing base construction budgets, enhancing long-term lease revenue potential. . “These projects reflect disciplined construction execution and close coordination with our hyperscale stakeholder and customers,” said Nazar Khan, Chief Technology Officer. . “Our teams are advancing build schedules, integrating tenant fit-out requirements, and optimizing cooling, electrical, and design architecture to support next-generation AI workloads at scale.”"
L000108330126000026_a_wulfearningsrelease2026-,fitout,1,flag,,,"Through design optimization across later phases, critical IT capacity for CB4 and CB5 increased from 162 MW to 168 MW per building without increasing base construction budgets, enhancing long-term lease revenue potential. . “These projects reflect disciplined construction execution and close coordination with our hyperscale stakeholder and customers,” said Nazar Khan, Chief Technology Officer. . “Our teams are advancing build schedules, integrating tenant fit-out requirements, and optimizing cooling, electrical, and design architecture to support next-generation AI workloads at scale.”"
L000108330126000026_a_wulfearningsrelease2026-,mw_gross,2900.0,MW,approximately,gross,"Subsequent to year-end, TeraWulf expects to expand its infrastructure portfolio through its acquisition of a site in Kentucky (MISO) and its planned acquisition of a site in Maryland (PJM), both strategically located brownfield sites, increasing total platform capacity to approximately 2.9 GW gross across five sites"
