L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,term_years,10.0,years,,,"(Nasdaq: WULF) (“TeraWulf” or the “Company”), a leading owner and operator of vertically integrated, predominantly zero-carbon digital infrastructure, today announced two 10-year high-performance computing (HPC) colocation agreements with Fluidstack, a premier AI cloud platform that builds and operates HPC clusters for some of the world’s largest companies"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,tenant,Fluidstack,,,,"(Nasdaq: WULF) (“TeraWulf” or the “Company”), a leading owner and operator of vertically integrated, predominantly zero-carbon digital infrastructure, today announced two 10-year high-performance computing (HPC) colocation agreements with Fluidstack, a premier AI cloud platform that builds and operates HPC clusters for some of the world’s largest companies"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,mw_it,200.0,MW,more than,it,"Under the agreements, TeraWulf will deliver more than 200 MW of critical IT load (representing ~250 MW of gross capacity) at its Lake Mariner data center campus in Western New York"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,mw_it,250.0,MW,~,it,"Under the agreements, TeraWulf will deliver more than 200 MW of critical IT load (representing ~250 MW of gross capacity) at its Lake Mariner data center campus in Western New York"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,contract_value,3700.0,$M,approximately,,"The agreements represent approximately $3.7 billion in contracted revenue over the initial 10-year terms and include two five-year extension options which, if exercised, would bring the total contract revenue to approximately $8.7 billion"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,contract_value,8700.0,$M,approximately,,"The agreements represent approximately $3.7 billion in contracted revenue over the initial 10-year terms and include two five-year extension options which, if exercised, would bring the total contract revenue to approximately $8.7 billion"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,term_years,10.0,years,,,"The agreements represent approximately $3.7 billion in contracted revenue over the initial 10-year terms and include two five-year extension options which, if exercised, would bring the total contract revenue to approximately $8.7 billion"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,term_years,5.0,years,,,"The agreements represent approximately $3.7 billion in contracted revenue over the initial 10-year terms and include two five-year extension options which, if exercised, would bring the total contract revenue to approximately $8.7 billion"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,financing_or_capex,1800.0,$M,,,"To support the buildout, Google will backstop $1.8 billion of Fluidstack’s lease obligations to support project-related debt financing and will receive warrants to acquire approximately 41 million shares of TeraWulf common stock, equating to an approximately 8% pro forma equity ownership stake—aligning TeraWulf with one of the most influential global AI partners"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,tenant,Fluidstack,,,,"To support the buildout, Google will backstop $1.8 billion of Fluidstack’s lease obligations to support project-related debt financing and will receive warrants to acquire approximately 41 million shares of TeraWulf common stock, equating to an approximately 8% pro forma equity ownership stake—aligning TeraWulf with one of the most influential global AI partners"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,tenant,Google,,,,"To support the buildout, Google will backstop $1.8 billion of Fluidstack’s lease obligations to support project-related debt financing and will receive warrants to acquire approximately 41 million shares of TeraWulf common stock, equating to an approximately 8% pro forma equity ownership stake—aligning TeraWulf with one of the most influential global AI partners"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,credit_support,1,flag,,,"To support the buildout, Google will backstop $1.8 billion of Fluidstack’s lease obligations to support project-related debt financing and will receive warrants to acquire approximately 41 million shares of TeraWulf common stock, equating to an approximately 8% pro forma equity ownership stake—aligning TeraWulf with one of the most influential global AI partners"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,tenant,Fluidstack,,,,An accompanying presentation regarding the Fluidstack transaction is available on the Company’s investor relations website at investors.terawulf.com
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,mw_it,40.0,MW,approximately,it,"Phase one—approximately 40 MW of critical IT load—is expected online in the first half of 2026, with the full 200+ MW deployed by year-end 2026, delivering substantial near-term capacity to Fluidstack"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,tenant,Fluidstack,,,,"Phase one—approximately 40 MW of critical IT load—is expected online in the first half of 2026, with the full 200+ MW deployed by year-end 2026, delivering substantial near-term capacity to Fluidstack"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,tenant,Fluidstack,,,,"This transaction underscores Lake Mariner’s status as a premier hyperscale-ready campus and further accelerates our strategic expansion into high-performance compute.”. . . . . . . . “Fluidstack’s commitment underscores the exceptional quality and readiness of our Lake Mariner facility and the capabilities of our team,” added Nazar Khan, Chief Technology Officer of TeraWulf. “With dual 345 kV transmission lines, closed-loop water cooling, and ultra-low-latency fiber connectivity, this campus is purpose-built for today’s most demanding AI workloads"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,tenant,Fluidstack,,,,"Our close collaboration with Fluidstack allowed us to design a fully customized, scalable solution.”. . “Fluidstack is proud to be a trusted provider of critical compute for the world’s leading AI labs,” said César Maklary, Co-Founder and President of Fluidstack. “Our partnership with TeraWulf reflects our shared commitment to delivering rapid, scalable infrastructure for the AI frontier.”"
L000110465925078084_tm2523008d2_ex99-1,contract_value,3700.0,$M,~,,Transaction Highlights . . · Contract Value: ~$3.7 billion across the initial 10-year terms . . · Lease Extensions: Two five-year options could increase total revenue to ~$8.7 billion . . · Lease Structure: Modified gross lease with annual escalators . . · Expected Site Net Operating Income (NOI) 1 Margins: 85% (implies ~$315 million annually) . . · Total Project Cost: $8-$10 million per MW of critical IT load . . · Google Participation: $1.8 billion backstop of Fluidstack lease obligations in support of project-related debt
