L000110465925104461_riot-20251030xex99d1,usd_other,12.6,$M,,,"The increase was primarily driven by a 52% increase in the average global network hash rate as compared to the same period in 2024, partially offset by a 147% increase in power credits received in Q3 2025 compared to power credits received in Q3 2024. . ● Bitcoin Mining revenue of $160.8 million for the quarter, as compared to $67.5 million for the same three-month period in 2024, primarily driven by higher average bitcoin prices and an increase in operational hash rate, partially offset by an increase in the average global network hash rate. . ● Engineering revenue of $19.1 million for the quarter, as compared to $12.6 million for the same three-month period in 2024"
L000110465925104461_riot-20251030xex99d1,financing_or_capex,23.0,$M,,,"Riot has realized $23.0 million in capex savings alone since the acquisition of ESS Metron in December 2021, demonstrating one of the key synergies resulting from this strategic operational asset. . ● Net income of $104.5 million or $0.26 Diluted EPS, as compared to a net loss of $154.4 million or $(0.54) Diluted EPS in the same three-month period in 2024. . ● Non-GAAP Adjusted EBITDA of $197.2 million for the quarter, which included a $133.1 million gain on Bitcoin held on the balance sheet. . ● Maintained industry-leading financial position, with $170.0 million in working capital, including $330.7 million in unrestricted cash on hand, and $75.6 million in restricted cash. . ● Held 19,287 bitcoin (of which 3,300 are currently held as collateral), equating to approximately $2.2 billion based on a market price for one bitcoin on September 30, 2025, of $114,068"
