L000114487925000005_apldq225earningsrelease,financing_or_capex,5000.0,$M,,,"• Applied Digital Corporation entered today into a $5.0 billion perpetual preferred equity financing facility, with investment vehicles of funds managed by Macquarie Asset Management (“MAM”), for its HPC business conducted through APLD HPC Holdings LLC (“APLDH”), a subsidiary of Applied Digital. . ◦ Funds managed by MAM to invest up to $900 million in the Company’s Ellendale HPC data center campus (the “Ellendale HPC Campus”). . ◦ Agreement to provide MAM a right to invest up to an additional $4.1 billion across Applied Digital’s future HPC data center pipeline. . ◦ The MAM investment, in conjunction with future project financing, to be used to repay project-level debt and allow the Company to recover over an estimated $300 million of its equity investment in the Ellendale HPC Campus. . ◦ MAM’s investment will take the form of a perpetual preferred and 15% common equity interest of Applied Digital’s HPC business segment, providing Applied Digital an 85% ownership stake in both existing and future HPC assets (minimizing dilution to Applied Digital’s public stockholders). . ◦ Transformative agreement positions the Company to firmly establish itself as a top-tier HPC data center designer, builder and operator in the United States with its purpose-built and proprietary design to run advanced AI workloads for both training and inference"
L000114487925000005_apldq225earningsrelease,usd_other,900.0,$M,up to,,"• Applied Digital Corporation entered today into a $5.0 billion perpetual preferred equity financing facility, with investment vehicles of funds managed by Macquarie Asset Management (“MAM”), for its HPC business conducted through APLD HPC Holdings LLC (“APLDH”), a subsidiary of Applied Digital. . ◦ Funds managed by MAM to invest up to $900 million in the Company’s Ellendale HPC data center campus (the “Ellendale HPC Campus”). . ◦ Agreement to provide MAM a right to invest up to an additional $4.1 billion across Applied Digital’s future HPC data center pipeline. . ◦ The MAM investment, in conjunction with future project financing, to be used to repay project-level debt and allow the Company to recover over an estimated $300 million of its equity investment in the Ellendale HPC Campus. . ◦ MAM’s investment will take the form of a perpetual preferred and 15% common equity interest of Applied Digital’s HPC business segment, providing Applied Digital an 85% ownership stake in both existing and future HPC assets (minimizing dilution to Applied Digital’s public stockholders). . ◦ Transformative agreement positions the Company to firmly establish itself as a top-tier HPC data center designer, builder and operator in the United States with its purpose-built and proprietary design to run advanced AI workloads for both training and inference"
L000114487925000005_apldq225earningsrelease,usd_other,4100.0,$M,,,"• Applied Digital Corporation entered today into a $5.0 billion perpetual preferred equity financing facility, with investment vehicles of funds managed by Macquarie Asset Management (“MAM”), for its HPC business conducted through APLD HPC Holdings LLC (“APLDH”), a subsidiary of Applied Digital. . ◦ Funds managed by MAM to invest up to $900 million in the Company’s Ellendale HPC data center campus (the “Ellendale HPC Campus”). . ◦ Agreement to provide MAM a right to invest up to an additional $4.1 billion across Applied Digital’s future HPC data center pipeline. . ◦ The MAM investment, in conjunction with future project financing, to be used to repay project-level debt and allow the Company to recover over an estimated $300 million of its equity investment in the Ellendale HPC Campus. . ◦ MAM’s investment will take the form of a perpetual preferred and 15% common equity interest of Applied Digital’s HPC business segment, providing Applied Digital an 85% ownership stake in both existing and future HPC assets (minimizing dilution to Applied Digital’s public stockholders). . ◦ Transformative agreement positions the Company to firmly establish itself as a top-tier HPC data center designer, builder and operator in the United States with its purpose-built and proprietary design to run advanced AI workloads for both training and inference"
L000114487925000005_apldq225earningsrelease,usd_other,300.0,$M,,,"• Applied Digital Corporation entered today into a $5.0 billion perpetual preferred equity financing facility, with investment vehicles of funds managed by Macquarie Asset Management (“MAM”), for its HPC business conducted through APLD HPC Holdings LLC (“APLDH”), a subsidiary of Applied Digital. . ◦ Funds managed by MAM to invest up to $900 million in the Company’s Ellendale HPC data center campus (the “Ellendale HPC Campus”). . ◦ Agreement to provide MAM a right to invest up to an additional $4.1 billion across Applied Digital’s future HPC data center pipeline. . ◦ The MAM investment, in conjunction with future project financing, to be used to repay project-level debt and allow the Company to recover over an estimated $300 million of its equity investment in the Ellendale HPC Campus. . ◦ MAM’s investment will take the form of a perpetual preferred and 15% common equity interest of Applied Digital’s HPC business segment, providing Applied Digital an 85% ownership stake in both existing and future HPC assets (minimizing dilution to Applied Digital’s public stockholders). . ◦ Transformative agreement positions the Company to firmly establish itself as a top-tier HPC data center designer, builder and operator in the United States with its purpose-built and proprietary design to run advanced AI workloads for both training and inference"
