L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,mw_unspecified,16.5,MW,,unspecified,"The Austin campus (“Austin Campus”) is a single building comprising two data halls that serve as a 16.5 MW data center located at 3301 Hibbetts Road in Austin, Texas on approximately 38 acres and is leased by Core Scientific from SDC—Austin, LLC (“Landlord” and the lease agreement, as amended, the “Austin Lease”)"
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,rfs,1,flag,,,The initial term of the Austin Lease commenced in March 2024 and is approximately 84 months long
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,rfs,1,flag,,,The term for each of Suite 1 and Suite 2 commenced in March 2024
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,tenant,CoreWeave,,,,CoreWeave did not materially contribute to the buildout costs
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,tenant,CoreWeave,,,,The commencement date under the Austin Colocation License Agreement occurred in the second quarter of 2024 and the obligation for CoreWeave to pay base license fees has commenced
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,rfs,1,flag,,,The commencement date under the Austin Colocation License Agreement occurred in the second quarter of 2024 and the obligation for CoreWeave to pay base license fees has commenced
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,mw_unspecified,262.0,MW,,unspecified,"The Denton campus (“Denton Campus”) is located at 8171 Jim Christal Road in Denton, Texas on property owned by the City of Denton and leased to Core Scientific (the “Denton Ground Lease”) totaling approximately 64 acres to accommodate the initial development of a 262 MW data center and subsequent conversion of the campus from cryptocurrency mining to HPC and AI workloads"
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,mw_unspecified,132.0,MW,approximately,unspecified,"Buildings D, E, F and G (approximately 132 MW) are currently operational and billing, with substantial completion of remaining MWs expected to occur in the second half of 2026"
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Construction of the multi-building HPC campus is being managed by T5 Construction, LLC (“T5”) pursuant to a contract where the basis of payment is the cost of the work plus a fee with a guaranteed maximum price, subject to additions and deductions by change order"
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,tenant,CoreWeave,,,,Certain costs and expenses relating to the construction of the Denton Campus are to be paid for or reimbursed by CoreWeave as described below
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,rfs,1,flag,,,The work commenced in the third quarter of 2024 and substantial completion is expected in the second half of 2026
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,mw_unspecified,394.0,MW,approximately,unspecified,"Power for the Denton Campus is supplied by the City of Denton through its municipal electric utility, Denton Municipal Electric (“DME”), pursuant to a power purchase agreement (as amended, the “DME Contract”), for a total potential campus load of approximately 394 MW"
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,term_years,7.0,years,,,"The DME Contract term is 14 years, with two additional seven-year extension options available upon one year’s written notice to DME, provided that the Denton Ground Lease must also be extended or renewed for the same amount of time"
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,mw_unspecified,30.0,MW,,unspecified,"Dalton 1 will feature a 30 MW data center, and construction involves converting the Property from cryptocurrency mining to HPC and AI workloads"
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,mw_unspecified,145.0,MW,,unspecified,Dalton 4 will feature a 145 MW data center and is a greenfield development
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,rfs,1,flag,,,"The process to transfer the Dalton Bonds is an administrative process that does not require the consent of the Dalton-Whitfield JDA or the applicable indenture trustee, which Core Scientific has commenced with the applicable indenture trustee and expects to complete promptly following the closing of the Offering"
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,credit_support,1,flag,,,They are limited obligations that are payable solely from the lease payments under the applicable Dalton Ground Lease and are guaranteed by Core Scientific
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,rfs,1,flag,,,The commencement date under the Dalton 1 Colocation License Agreement is expected to occur in the first half of 2026
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,rfs,1,flag,,,The commencement date under the Dalton 4 Colocation License Agreement is expected to occur in the second half of 2026
L000119312526165121_d149019dex992,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Construction for Dalton 1 is being managed by T5 pursuant to a contract where the basis of payment is the cost of the work plus a fee with a guaranteed maximum price, subject to additions and deductions by change order"
