L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,contract_value,1500.0,$M,approximately,,(NASDAQ: FIP) (“FTAI Infrastructure”) for a total transaction value of approximately $1.5 billion (including the assumption of certain debt)
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,mw_unspecified,505.0,MW,,unspecified,"The acquisition includes Long Ridge Energy’s highly efficient 505 MW 2 nameplate combined-cycle gas power plant (the “Long Ridge CCGT”) in Hannibal, Ohio, and over 1,600 contiguous acres supporting an integrated digital infrastructure campus in one of the most active data center and power markets in the world"
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,mw_unspecified,1000.0,MW,more than,unspecified,"The acquired campus will provide immediate access to power, land, water and fiber upon closing, with less site development execution risk relative to greenfield alternatives, and supports more than 1 GW of total potential power capacity across generation and load"
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,mw_unspecified,2200.0,MW,approximately,unspecified,"With the acquisition, MARA will expand its operational and development capacity to approximately 2.2 gigawatts across the PJM, ERCOT, SPP, and international markets"
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,credit_support,1,flag,,,"MARA’s Hannibal data center, co-located at the Long Ridge Energy site, has already received inbound interest from multiple potential investment-grade AI/Critical IT tenants"
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,mw_it,200.0,MW,,it,"MARA expects construction of an initial AI/Critical IT buildout to begin in 1H 2027, with initial capacity accelerated by its current 200 MW of capacity and targeted to be ready for service in mid-2028"
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,rfs,1,flag,,,"MARA expects construction of an initial AI/Critical IT buildout to begin in 1H 2027, with initial capacity accelerated by its current 200 MW of capacity and targeted to be ready for service in mid-2028"
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,mw_unspecified,485.0,MW,,unspecified,Refer to “Non-GAAP Financial Information” for the definitions of such terms and reconciliations to the closest comparable GAAP metrics. . . 2 Currently authorized to sell 485 MW; expected to increase to full 505 MW nameplate in H2 2026
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,mw_unspecified,505.0,MW,,unspecified,Refer to “Non-GAAP Financial Information” for the definitions of such terms and reconciliations to the closest comparable GAAP metrics. . . 2 Currently authorized to sell 485 MW; expected to increase to full 505 MW nameplate in H2 2026
L000119312526193982_d54802dex991,mw_gross,505.0,MW,~,gross,"In addition, the Long Ridge CCGT maintains approximately 125 acres of industrially permitted land and is a highly efficient combined-cycle gas turbine in the PJM interconnection, with ~505 MW and approximately 100 MMcfd of vertically integrated fuel supply"
