L000121390026080199_ea029866401ex99-2,rfs,1,flag,,,"Power Economics • Predictable, contracted energy pricing; reduced exposure to congestion pricing, demand charges, and curtailment risk • Modular MW-block deployment aligned to leasing for rapid energization and scalable expansion • Integrated power + optimized cooling supports lower total delivered $/kW and improved operating leverage Reliability & Control • Utility-independent uptime and enterprise- grade SLAs for hyperscale and AI workloads • Reduced exposure to grid outages, congestion events, load shedding, and interconnection delays • Purpose-built turbine-led and microgrid- ready architectures with layered redundancy for always-on compute vs"
L000121390026080199_ea029866401ex99-2,mw_unspecified,300.0,MW,,unspecified,"Expedited Deployment On-Site Power & Resilience Community Impact • 300 MW Phase I goal is to be operational in 18–24 months, with ambition to scale to up to 1.1 GW IT load • Phases 2-5: 5-year goal to achieve full build out of up to 3 GW (1) total • Adaptive reuse: Shuttered industrial site transformed into AI-ready campus— minimizing disruption • Significantly faster than the average greenfield construction via existing zoning, shell, and utility access • 675+ MW (2) potential tenant pipeline • Aiming to achieve 99.999% uptime via on- site natural gas-fired microgrids with layered redundancy • Significantly lower CapEx through turnkey microgrid integration vs. traditional builds • Grid-independent: Eliminates utility queue backlogs, congestion pricing, and interconnection delays • Clean energy aligned: Low-emission turbines supporting Pennsylvania clean energy goals under Title 17 • Resilient by design: Strengths during peak demand or outages, not vulnerabilities • Investment across construction, power generation, and tenancy • Construction jobs expected to be created in Years 1–2"
L000121390026080199_ea029866401ex99-2,mw_it,1100.0,MW,up to,it,"Expedited Deployment On-Site Power & Resilience Community Impact • 300 MW Phase I goal is to be operational in 18–24 months, with ambition to scale to up to 1.1 GW IT load • Phases 2-5: 5-year goal to achieve full build out of up to 3 GW (1) total • Adaptive reuse: Shuttered industrial site transformed into AI-ready campus— minimizing disruption • Significantly faster than the average greenfield construction via existing zoning, shell, and utility access • 675+ MW (2) potential tenant pipeline • Aiming to achieve 99.999% uptime via on- site natural gas-fired microgrids with layered redundancy • Significantly lower CapEx through turnkey microgrid integration vs. traditional builds • Grid-independent: Eliminates utility queue backlogs, congestion pricing, and interconnection delays • Clean energy aligned: Low-emission turbines supporting Pennsylvania clean energy goals under Title 17 • Resilient by design: Strengths during peak demand or outages, not vulnerabilities • Investment across construction, power generation, and tenancy • Construction jobs expected to be created in Years 1–2"
