L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,usd_other,10000.0,$M,,,"In 2025, access to the international debt capital markets remained strong, with Shell's debt principally financed from these markets through central debt programmes consisting of: ￮ two $10 billion commercial paper (CP) programmes, with maturities between 183 days and 364 days depending on the form of the notes issued; ￮ an unlimited Euro medium-term note (EMTN) programme (also referred to as the Multi-Currency Debt Securities Programme), which lapsed in November 2024, and was renewed in May 2025; and ￮ an unlimited US universal shelf (US shelf) registration"
L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,credit_support,1,flag,,,"The debt issued under the CP, EMTN and US shelf has historically been issued by Shell International Finance B.V., the primary issuance company for Shell, with its debt being guaranteed by Shell plc"
L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,credit_support,1,flag,,,"Additionally, Shell Finance US Inc. issued new debt in November 2025, which is guaranteed by Shell plc"
L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,credit_support,1,flag,,,"We expect any new debt issued under the CP programmes, EMTN or US shelf to be guaranteed by Shell plc"
L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,financing_or_capex,8000.0,$M,,,"We also maintain an $8 billion committed credit facility with initial maturity in 2030, however extension options may take final maturity to 2032"
L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,financing_or_capex,8000.0,$M,,,This facility replaces the previous $8 billion facility due to mature in December 2026
L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,contract_value,1400.0,$M,,,"Our total debt decreased by $1.4 billion to $75.6 billion at December 31, 2025"
L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,contract_value,75600.0,$M,,,"Our total debt decreased by $1.4 billion to $75.6 billion at December 31, 2025"
L000162828026017027_shellannualreportandacco,usd_other,2350.0,$M,,,"In 2025, we did not issue any debt under the EMTN programme or CP programmes, while issuing $2.35 billion under the US shelf"
